cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ActionsBench, please cite it as below and state the corpus version you used."
title: "ActionsBench: a labeled benchmark for GitHub Actions workflow security scanners"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Tijani
    given-names: Aliu
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NeesimEra/ActionsBench"
url: "https://github.com/NeesimEra/ActionsBench"
abstract: >-
  A labeled corpus of minimized GitHub Actions workflows, each tagged with the weakness it contains or marked
  clean, and a harness that scores workflow security scanners against it per weakness class. The corpus is
  licensed CC BY 4.0, which is the license named here, and the harness code is licensed MIT; both licenses
  ship with the package. Version 0.1.1 is an initial release (pre-1.0) of 44 hand-built cases: all labels are
  proposed by one author and audited against primary sources, but not independently reviewed.
keywords:
  - github-actions
  - security
  - benchmark
  - static-analysis
